{"case_id":"C055","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","entry point compatibility"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["gif_fuzzer.c::fuzz","zlib_fuzzer.c::fuzz"],"reason":"S1 changes wuffs_base__status from const char* to a struct containing repr, but both H0 fuzz entry points still store decoder results in const char* and use pointer-style status comparisons and returns. This makes H0 incompatible with the S1 API and prevents it from adequately reaching the changed GIF and zlib decoder behavior. S0 used typedef const char* wuffs_base__status, so the incompatibility is introduced by this commit.","evidence":["In S0, core-public.h and wuffs-unsupported-snapshot.c define typedef const char* wuffs_base__status; S1 replaces it with typedef struct { const char* repr; ... } wuffs_base__status.","gif_fuzzer.c::fuzz declares const char* status and assigns wuffs_gif__decoder__initialize, wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_image_config, wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame_config, and wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame results to it.","zlib_fuzzer.c::fuzz declares const char* status and assigns results from wuffs_zlib__decoder__initialize and wuffs_zlib__decoder__decode_io_writer to it.","H0 compares status directly with wuffs_base__warning__end_of_data and wuffs_base__suspension__short_write and returns status as const char*, while S1 status values require access through repr or the pointer-taking wuffs_base__status__* helpers."],"recommended_action":"Update both fuzz functions to use wuffs_base__status for decoder results, inspect statuses through status.repr or the S1 wuffs_base__status__* helpers, compare warning and suspension identifiers through repr, and return the underlying repr to preserve the fuzz entry-point contract."}
